@startuml dependencies

title TODO Application - Dependency Flow (Layered Architecture)

skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam padding 10

left to right direction

' Layer 5: CLI - topmost
rectangle "Layer 5: CLI" #FFE5E5 [
    <b>TodoCLI</b>
    <b>InteractiveMenu</b>
]

' Layer 4: Services
rectangle "Layer 4: Services" #DDFFD4 [
    <b>TodoService</b> (orchestrator)
    ----
    <b>TaskManager</b>
    <b>CommentsService</b>
    <b>ProjectManager</b>
    <b>ImportExportService</b>
]

' Layer 3: Domain
rectangle "Layer 3: Domain Repositories" #FFE5CC [
    <b>TaskRepositoryImpl</b>
    <b>CommentRepositoryImpl</b>
    <b>ProjectRepositoryImpl</b>
]

' Layer 2: Protocols (abstract)
rectangle "Layer 2: Protocol Contracts" #EEEEFF [
    <b><<protocol>></b>
    TaskRepository
    CommentRepository
    ProjectRepository
    StorageBackend
]

' Layer 1: Storage
rectangle "Layer 1: Storage Backend" #FFF3CC [
    <b>JsonStorage</b>
    (implements StorageBackend)
]

' Layer 0: Models - bottom, no dependencies
rectangle "Layer 0: Domain Models" #DDEEFF [
    <b>Task</b> | <b>Project</b>
    <b>TaskComment</b> | <b>TaskStatus</b>
    <b>FilterOptions</b> | <b>TaskSummary</b>
]

' Dependencies: top to bottom
"Layer 5: CLI" --> "Layer 4: Services" : uses
"Layer 4: Services" --> "Layer 3: Domain Repositories" : uses
"Layer 3: Domain Repositories" --> "Layer 2: Protocol Contracts" : implements
"Layer 2: Protocol Contracts" --> "Layer 1: Storage Backend" : defined by
"Layer 1: Storage Backend" --> "Layer 0: Domain Models" : serializes
"Layer 3: Domain Repositories" --> "Layer 0: Domain Models" : operates on
"Layer 4: Services" --> "Layer 0: Domain Models" : uses

note right of "Layer 3: Domain Repositories"
    TaskRepositoryImpl, CommentRepositoryImpl, and
    ProjectRepositoryImpl each implement their
    corresponding Protocol, depending on
    StorageBackend abstraction (not concrete JsonStorage)
end note

note right of "Layer 2: Protocol Contracts"
    Protocols define the contract between
    Domain and Storage layers.
    They enable dependency injection and
    decouple implementation from abstraction.
end note

note right of "Layer 1: Storage Backend"
    JsonStorage implements all StorageBackend
    methods. It is the only concrete storage
    implementation in the system.
end note

@enduml
